(1) Please express y as a function of x;
(2) At what selling price will the total profit be maximized, and what is the profit at this price?

s:
(1) The profit function y can be expressed as $y = (100 + x - 80) \cdot (1000 - 10x) = -10x^2 + 800x + 20000$, where $0 \leq x \leq 100$, $x \in \mathbb{N}$;
(2) Since the axis of symmetry of the quadratic function y is at $x = 40$, the function y reaches its maximum value when $x = 40$; thus, $y_{\text{max}} = -10 \times 1600 + 800 \times 40 + 20000 = 36000$.
Therefore, when the selling price is set at 140 yuan, the profit is maximized, and the maximum profit is $\boxed{36000}$ yuan.

